Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:13:51 +0000

A client that syncs the list from lab-mail needs a notmuch setup of
its own. The tags must come from the folders, since the folder a
message is in is its state on the list, and replied must not flap,
since flag sync mirrors it to a file name that mbsync pushes back.

A separate profile lets that setup be tried beside the default one,
which still reads the jj maildir, so nothing changes until a client
is pointed at it.

- lab-mail/config.sample becomes ~/.config/notmuch/lab-mail/config
  if none exists, with flag sync on for Pat.
- Its post-new hook derives sent, replied, inbox, next, later, and
  archived, and changes replied only where it is wrong.
- Its pre-new hook removes deleted drafts and never fetches.
